  "root_mathematical_review": {
    "strong_pair_derivation": "For the same ordered background and complete pure SPE, let F(X)=sum_X1/(b+1), G(X,Y)=sum_intersection1/((b+1)(b+2)), U=F-G, H=U(C,D)+U(D,C)+G(C,C). With J the true last reply after forced T, the three genuine IC slacks I1=U(C,D)-U(T,J), I2=U(J,T)-U(Q,T), I3=U(D,C)-U(J,C) give H-F(T)-F(Q)+G(T,Q)=I1+I2+I3+G(C,C)-G(C,J)>=0. Q is any legal common-catalogue label, not necessarily optimal. The last nonnegative term is supported on C\\J. This eliminates the unspecified true J without freezing continuation or assuming clientwise IC.",
    "mixed_scope": "The fixed1905-column point has1K+16hist+582joint+1306overlap columns. The00 joint mass is implicit. Ordered group multiplicities are30,30,6, including distinct indices with the same word. Two member choices, three groups and twelve Q labels produce72 necessary rows; each class pays its own n_g H. All eight old alpha=mu=1 last-node cuts map with qi+6 to three already-present mixed vectors. No duplicate direction is claimed.",
    "fixed_z_noncompletion": "The seven saved negative keys for the exact f6f4d5c28857e8e6350bdc8528daa6109122bce8a6fb00e8ac5c3150ffc42314 point all read only memberZ. Fixed hist and the related Z=y01+y11 group marginals preserve the negative value, even while R marginals, R/Z coupling, K, old overlaps, catalogue extensions and unrecorded true replies vary. Thus no full pure SPE can realize those normalized marginals. This does not prohibit all hist-only or same-W completions. The old191 Frechet violations are a different defect: raising overlap variables may repair them but cannot affect a row with zero K/overlap coefficients.",
    "minor_and_scaling": "The original zero-based columns118,142,145,151,166,169 give a six-row minor [-6] direct-sum [[-6,-6,-6],[-3,-3,-6],[-6,-3,-6]] direct-sum [[-3,-2],[-3,-1]], determinant(-6)(-54)(-3)=-972. Six full-coordinate row vectors are independent; this is not independence modulo the old4963 constraints, facetness or nonredundancy in a cone. Positive O normalization and positive integer clearing of rational denominators preserve the negative sign, so the obstruction is mathematical and not a ban on fractional representations.",
    "floor_contribution_limit": "The strongPAIR source plus exact fixed-point negative evidence pays the necessary-row identification and normalized marginal noncompletion part of the target. It does not by itself prove existence, O/W/168 positive columns or feasibility of all4927+36 original rows. Those retain the original mature record and Boss1 full-record reading attribution. No negative is transported to4971/5043/5287 points with different hidden data.",
    "mutation_static_application": "For the exact nine-type215899-client point and actual30000, frozen payoffs over labels0..6 are (23996,23996,23996,23996,23991,23996,23996) for the first3 player and (24001,24001,24001,23986,23996,23986,24001) for each0 player. The actual choices maximize both lists, paying all35 static comparisons. The static PNE theorem therefore applies to this instance and gives OPT5<=2W, with W120000, unique optimal five-label support12456 and OPT215899, half margin24101. Positive private types force that support; it covers every type. Full2801-node qualification,16806 nonself IC and d1000 remain separate original obligations/evidence.",
    "mutation_stronger_static_bound": "The newly reviewed general static averaging proof gives OPT_m<=(2-1/m)W, so this finite point satisfies OPT5<=216000 with exact gap101. Indeed mW>=sum_ij u_i(T_j,a_-i); an uncovered optimal customer contributes at least m and a covered optimal customer at least1, so mW>=mU+O and OPT<=W+(1-1/m)O<=(2-1/m)W. This is an additional integration explanation, not a silent change of the finite target or a new claim that its old edge records this stronger whole theorem.",
    "fixed_sigma_corollary": "For the exact default0/nine-exception mutation sigma, every forced branch at the five actual prefixes has its old zero suffix: root forced a goes a0000 and avoids004/066 and the depth4 exceptions, while later actual prefixes start3 and no nonroot exception does. Thus all35 actual true IC are static IC for every mass vector. Any full-history feasible mass vector for this same sigma has OPT5<=9W/5. A relabeled nine-client baseline n_{0,2,3}=5 and n_{1}=n_{4}=n_{5}=n_{6}=1 makes every sigma action a big-block action. At every history its payoff5/(nu+r)>=1 dominates private actions, proving full SPE analytically and attaining W5/OPT9. This fixed-sigma cone result is support/integration only, not a new edge/object or a claim about other sigma with the same leaf.",
    "distinct_overlay_boundary": "Adding t nonnegative integer copies of that baseline to the frozen seven-distinct point preserves fixed-sigma IC by linearity, unique support12456, W120000+5t and OPT215899+9t. The ratio is9/5-101/(120000+5t). All seven sets remain distinct and min symmetric difference stays120. The d1000 constraint therefore holds only at t0; the limiting sharpness is outside that fixed separation constraint. No all-SPE optimum for the original finite instance follows.",
    "root_reading": "Root read both complete new edges, both target contracts, all packet support and exact receipt coverage. Root independently reconstructed the strongPAIR three-IC sum, old-cut identity, Z-only dependence and block determinant from the full original lemma/program/point bodies. Root read the entire original nine-type mutation body and independently checked the two payoff cases, private-type optimum, actual-branch suffix argument, baseline SPE and linear overlay. Fresh auditors independently checked the local Fraction minor and14 payoffs/35 branch identities. Boss1 retains full original large-array reading and mature execution attribution; neither Root nor these auditors reran or claimed a fresh full audit of those large scientific arrays.",
    "remaining": "These two new contributions do not resolve exact-six or universal sequential half, general full terminal tax, aggregate/commonQ payment, or a general SPE-to-static-PNE bridge. There are no formal overlap follow-ups in either definition. Ordered-path preservation is correctly separated from all-history IC, input identity, separation constraints and global optimality."
